From: YuZora kernel porter <kartik@aoisora.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] msm/npu: fix npu_debugfs.o dropped by := overwrite in Makefile

drivers/media/platform/msm/npu/npu_dev.c:2231: undefined reference
to `npu_debugfs_init' (in npu_probe) and npu_dev.c:2290: undefined
reference to `npu_debugfs_deinit' (in npu_remove) at the vmlinux
link, kernel build run #4, 2026-11-24, Gate 3.

Root cause: the NPU Makefile builds the debugfs file and the
driver with `:=` on the same obj-y variable:

    obj-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_FS)     := npu_debugfs.o
    obj-$(CONFIG_MSM_NPU)      := msm_npu.o

With CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y and CONFIG_MSM_NPU=y (both set in
kernel/m51_defconfig) both lines expand to obj-y, and the second
`:=` assignment overwrites the first — npu_debugfs.o is never
compiled. The run #4 log proves it: all five msm_npu-objs members
were compiled (log lines 3230-3245) but there is no `CC ...
npu_debugfs.o` line anywhere, while npu_dev.c calls the two
functions under `#ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS` and npu_common.h declares
them the same way, so the references exist with no defining
object. The same `:=` form is also broken the other way round
(MSM_NPU=m leaves a module referencing a non-exported symbol).

Fix: `:=` -> `+=` on both lines, so both objects land in obj-y.
No behaviour change beyond building the file the driver already
calls. The parent Makefile already enters npu/ with
`obj-$(CONFIG_MSM_NPU) += npu/`, so no change is needed there.

Applies to kkisdevil/android_kernel_samsung_sm7150 @ 4d83f24b
(crDroid 4.14.357-openela). Applied porter-side by the
build-kernel workflow (patches/kernel/*.patch) so the pinned
kernel ref stays untouched.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/npu/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/npu/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
-obj-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_FS)     := npu_debugfs.o
-obj-$(CONFIG_MSM_NPU)      := msm_npu.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_FS)     += npu_debugfs.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_MSM_NPU)      += msm_npu.o
 msm_npu-objs := npu_dbg.o \
